    "collective_statement_most_likely_to_succeed": "Candidate 3 (COMPREHENSIVE) is the most likely to succeed because it explicitly and accurately identifies the specific pre-examination notices it is responding to (the Notice to File Missing Parts mailed April 20, 2026, and the Notice of Incomplete Reply mailed August 6, 2026). This establishes a clear procedural nexus for the Office of Patent Application Processing (OPAP) to clear the pre-examination formalities. Furthermore, it correctly assesses the factual record by noting that all required fees were already satisfied via electronic payment on October 15, 2026, rather than attempting to apply credits to already-paid fees. It also successfully executes the highly rewarded preemptive strike of filing a Substitute Specification to excise embedded drawings, segregate claims and abstract, and delete the Statement of License Grant to preserve Small Entity status, fully complying with 37 CFR 1.58, 1.72, 1.75, and 1.125.",
    "unlikely_to_succeed_reasons": null,
    "ats_alignment_assessment": "The candidate correctly deviates from the outdated Waterfall Strategy Directive (which assumed 0 months extension and unpaid fees) and instead aligns with the actual docket XML state and the Attorney Summary, which confirm that all fees were paid on October 15, 2026. It successfully addresses all cited deficiencies, requests the refund/credit of the unapplied $416.00 deposit, and preemptively cures formal defects as mandated.",
